      "position": [
        260,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "q1",
              "name": "question",
              "value": "Are we still shipping the new onboarding flow?",
              "type": "string"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Set question",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        480,
        300
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "endpointUrl": "https://app.rithmo.ai/api/mcp",
        "serverTransport": "httpStreamable",
        "authentication": "bearerAuth",
        "tool": {
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "query_decision",
          "cachedResultName": "query_decision"
        },
        "inputMode": "json",
        "jsonInput": "={{ { \"question\": $json.question } }}"
      },
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Rithmo: query_decision",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.mcpClient",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        720,
        300
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "httpBearerAuth": {
          "id": "REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_CREDENTIAL_ID",
          "name": "Rithmo MCP token"
        }
      },
      "notes": "Create an HTTP Bearer Auth credential holding your rmcp_... token and select it here."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c1",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.structuredContent.result === \"found\" || ($json.structuredContent.result === \"found_record\" && $json.structuredContent.subject.currentAnswer !== null && String($json.structuredContent.subject.currentAnswer).trim() !== \"\") }}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "IF usable answer on record",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        960,
        300
      ],
      "notes": "Proceeds on found, or on found_record ONLY when subject.currentAnswer is a non-null, non-blank string. A found_record with no answer text is on record but not actionable, so it holds."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
      "name": "Proceed (act on the decision)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1420,
        200
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000006",
      "name": "Hold (no answer to act on)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1180,
        400
      ],
      "notes": "Reached by no_record, and by found_record with a null/blank currentAnswer. On no_record, structuredContent.record may carry a typed refusal whose premise_check.safe_to_proceed is always false. Do not act."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Rithmo: query_decision before acting\n\n1. In **Rithmo: query_decision**, set the MCP Endpoint URL and an **HTTP Bearer Auth** credential holding your `rmcp_...` token (Server Transport = HTTP Streamable).\n2. `query_decision` returns THREE result variants: `found`, `found_record`, and `no_record`.\n   Do NOT branch on `result == \"found\"` alone - that sends valid `found_record` answers down the hold path.\n3. The **IF** node proceeds only on a USABLE answer: `found`, or `found_record` whose `subject.currentAnswer` is non-null and non-blank. A `found_record` can name a subject that is genuinely on record while carrying no answer text - that holds.\n4. **Extract answer** normalises the two shapes: `found` -> `answer`, `found_record` -> `subject.currentAnswer`.\n5. On `no_record`, `structuredContent.record` may carry a typed refusal (`closed` / `no_record` / `not_observed`) whose `premise_check.safe_to_proceed` is always false. Hold - do not act.\n6. Replace the NoOp nodes with your real actions.",
        "height": 470,
        "width": 380
      },
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007",
      "name": "Setup notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        260,
        460
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "a1",
              "name": "answer",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.structuredContent.result === \"found\" ? $json.structuredContent.answer : $json.structuredContent.subject.currentAnswer }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "a2",
              "name": "answer_source",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "={{ $json.structuredContent.result }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000008",
      "name": "Extract answer (found | found_record)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [
        1180,
        200
      ],
      "notes": "Reached only when the IF confirmed a usable answer. found -> answer ; found_record -> subject.currentAnswer (already checked non-null)."
    }
  ],
